Author: Jean-Eudes Dazard [aut, cre], Hua Xu [ctb], Alberto Santana
        [ctb]
Maintainer: Jean-Eudes Dazard <jean-eudes.dazard@case.edu>
Description: This is a non-parametric method for joint adaptive
        mean-variance regularization and variance stabilization of
        high-dimensional data. It is suited for handling difficult
        problems posed by high-dimensional multivariate datasets (p >>
        n paradigm). Among those are that the variance is often a
        function of the mean, variable-specific estimators of variances
        are not reliable, and tests statistics have low powers due to a
        lack of degrees of freedom. Key features include: (i)
        Normalization and/or variance stabilization of the data, (ii)
        Computation of mean-variance-regularized t-statistics
        (F-statistics to follow), (iii) Generation of diverse
        diagnostic plots, (iv) Computationally efficient implementation
        using C/C++ interfacing and an option for parallel computing to
        enjoy a faster and easier experience in the R environment.
Depends: R (>= 3.0.2), statmod
Imports: parallel, methods
